# Leaguebound Stack & Philosophy

## Technical Stack
- **Framework:** React Native (Expo)
- **Language:** TypeScript (Strict mode)
- **Narrative:** inkjs (Ink)
- **State:** Zustand (local-first persistence)
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS (NativeWind)

## Granularity Protocol
- **Small batches only:** Break every task into Micro-Sprints. Never build a whole feature in one go.
- **Atomic components:** Keep UI components small. If a file exceeds 150 lines, suggest splitting it.
- **Verification first:** After every logic change, generate a simple test script to verify the math (e.g., sim 100 possessions to check shooting %).

## Ink Integration
- All narrative logic **MUST** live in `.ink` files.
- React should only **read state from Ink** and display it. No narrative branching or story logic in React/TS.
